In $\triangle ABC$ with sides $AC = BC = 4\sqrt{5}\ \text{cm}$, $CD$ $(D \in AB)$ is an altitude and $AD = 4\ \text{cm}$. Find:

A) the area of $\triangle ABC$;

B) the radius of the circle inscribed in $\triangle ABC$;

C) the radius of the circle circumscribed about $\triangle ABC$;

D) the length of the bisector $OL$ in $\triangle BOD$, where the point $O$ is the centre of the circle circumscribed about $\triangle ABC$.
